        "original_id": "be364a67-dde1-59b5-9967-b048e87f1091",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nelly Ben-Or, Frederick Matthias Alexander\n- Organizations: Guildhall School of Music and Drama\n- Roles: concert pianist, Professor\n- Concepts: Alexander Technique\n- Places: Lwow, Poland\n\nFacts:\n- Nelly Nechama Ben-Or, also known as Nelly Ben-Or Clynes, was born in 1933 in Lwow, Poland.\n- Since 1975, Nelly Ben-Or has taught piano and the Alexander Technique at the Guildhall School of Music and Drama as a Professor.\n- Nelly Ben-Or is an international concert pianist.\n- The Alexander Technique is an educational process named after Frederick Matthias Alexander.\n- The Alexander Technique attempts to develop the ability to avoid unnecessary muscular tension by retraining physical movement reactions.",
